                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Survival game where you have to explore some metro tunnels and have to find a way to escape while avoiding or fighting zombies.\n\nThis game is really frustrating. I will tell you why\n\n-The map is huge and very maze like, also a lot of the areas are looking the same.\n-You have to find a lot of items, the locations are always random, this sucks. Also there are some items, which you can just find once but there are two spots on the map to use them, which means you can't fully open all doors. (But you can still get to every location. Still this is stupid.)\n-There are two different ways to escape but before you can do that, besides finding some items, you have to find all 9 notes, which again have random locations. This is so stupid. I beat the game twice (needed 3 runs), on my third run, after some time I found all items to escape but haven't found all notes. So I searched almost the whole map again for one last note. This wouldn't be a problem, if the map wouldn't be so big and the locations would be more obvious.\nPlease developers: collectibles like notes are great, but make them optional, not mandatory.\n-The only survival aspect is the hunger. I have to say I don't like survial games and I didn't like the hunger system here. The system is just that you have a hunger bar which drains after time and to replenish it you have to find water or food cans. It creates kind off a timer and you are constantly stressed because of it. Add this to the fact that you need a lot of time to find all notes and needed items. And of course the amount of hunger items is limited.\n-The Zombies. There is only one weapon to fight them: the crowbar. But the location is random and it could be that it's almost at the end of the map. The crowbar sucks. You have just one attack. The problem is you die after 3 hits, health items are really rare and it's extremly hard to fight zombies and avoiding beeing hit. It's really a bad combat system.\nBUT Zombies are extremly slow and you usually can outrun and ignore them. The only problem is if you encounter zombies in little rooms, there it could be that they hit you. But in general they aren't a huge problem. Just avoid them and you are fine 99% of the time. It would be a better game without them. Same with the hunger.\n-The only way to save is by sleeping in a save room. But they are really rare, it takes a lot of time to find the first one and if you save it will cost you about half of the full hunger bar. I used this once or twice in my first run where I failed by the way because I couldn't find the needed items. And in my other runs I didn't even use the save system, because hunger items are too limited. Also in my last run this was bugged, for some reason I couldn't save. But of course this means if you die, you have to restart from the beginning. Permadeath always sucks.\nJust make a save system which does not punish you for using it and make more save rooms.\n\nI only recommend this to masochists.",
